    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #348\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to `bb/relay-232-auth-v1-03-08-record-login-attempts-an-thr_emp9qxe25r`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #232: records every login attempt with a normalized email and applies exponential lockout before password verification.\n\n- **`emailNormalization.ts`** — trims and lowercases the email once at `login()`'s entry, used consistently for the user lookup and every recorded attempt.\n- **`loginLockout.ts`** — `lockoutDurationSeconds`: zero below a 5-failure threshold, then doubles per failure past it (30s, 60s, 120s, ...), capped at 1 hour.\n- **`loginAttemptsStore.ts`** — new `getFailureStreak` counts consecutive failures for an email+IP pair since their last success, so a successful login naturally resets the lockout.\n- **`authActions.ts`** — `login()` checks the active lockout window before calling `verifyPassword`; while locked, even a correct password is rejected with the same generic `UnauthorizedError`, and the rejection is itself recorded as a failed attempt (extending the lockout on repeated retries).\n\nAdded unit tests for the lockout math and email normalization, plus integration tests covering: normalized-email recording, threshold rejection, no lockout below threshold, email+IP scoping, exponential growth, reset-after-success, and lockout lifting once the window elapses.\n\nVerified: unit (101/101), integration (718/718), e2e (5/5) all pass; lint, Prettier format check, and dependency-boundary check are clean.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
